         </p><a href=https://smashingconf.com/online-workshops/ role=button class="btn btn--white btn--large">Explore all speakers and topics&nbsp;&rarr;</a>
<a href=https://smashingconf.com/online-workshops/><img class="conf-panel__image conf-panel__image--blue" src=/images/events/online-workshops.svg width=920 height=518 loading=lazy alt="The Smashing Cat enjoying adventures, and the sun."></a></div></div></div></section><section class="curated-articles-container bg--white"><div class=container><div class="row col col--slim col-12"><h4 class="vertical vertical--white vertical--horizontal-fallback left-aligned"><span>Community Links</span></h4><div id=person-of-the-week class="col-12 f-article-highlights__person"><div class="flex flex-wrap"><div class="flex-0 mb-5 mr-5"><div class="mobw-40 mobh-40 w-64 h-64 rounded-xl bio-image__large"><figure role=presentation class=bio-image><a href=/person-of-the-week/christopher-nguyen/ class=bio-image-link><div class=bio-image-wrapper><picture><source width=100 height=100 type=image/avif srcset=https://files.smashing.media/person-of-the-week/chris-nguyen-250px.avif><img class=bio-image-image src=https://files.smashing.media/person-of-the-week/chris-nguyen-250px-opt.png loading=eager decoding=async fetchpriority=high width=100 height=100 alt="Christopher Nguyen, person of the week"></picture></div></a></figure></div></div><div class=md:flex-1><h4 class=author__desc__title>Person Of The Week</h4><p>Christopher Nguyen is a product designer, creator, and founder. With experience spanning Fortune 100 organizations and startup unicorns, he helps product teams and companies elevate their design practices and solve complex problems through workshops and sprints. Chris is passionate about making UX education digestible and fun. To support designers on their UX journey, he runs <a href=http://uxplaybook.org>UX Playbook</a>, shares free <a href=https://uxplaybook.org/freebies>UX resources</a>, writes a weekly <a href=https://newsletter.uxplaybook.org/>UX newsletter</a>, and hosts <a href=https://www.youtube.com/@UXChrisNguyen>livestreams with design experts</a>. Thank you for everything you do for the community, dear Chris!</p></div></div></div><div class="f-article-highlights article--grid__container col col--slim col-12"><div class=f-article-item><article class=article--post><header><div class="article--post__image rounded-lg w-20 h-20"><figure role=presentation class=bio-image><a href=https://pt.linkedin.com/in/fannyvassilatos class=bio-image-link><div class=bio-image-wrapper><img class=bio-image-image src=https://files.smashing.media/community-links/fanny-vassilatos-100px-opt.png loading=eager decoding=async fetchpriority=high width=100 height=100 alt="Fanny Vassilatos"></div></a></figure></div><span class=article--post__author-name><a class=red href=https://pt.linkedin.com/in/fannyvassilatos>Fanny Vassilatos</a>
<em class=light-grey>wrote</em></span></header><h2 class="article--post__title h1"><a href=https://www.pencilandpaper.io/articles/ux-pattern-analysis-loading-feedback>Loading Feedback</a></h2><div class=article--post__content><p class=article--post__teaser><time datetime=2026-02-05 class=article--post__time>February 5, 2026 —</time>
How can you reduce the perceived wait time for users? Fanny Vassilatos and Ceara Crawshaw explore <a href=https://www.pencilandpaper.io/articles/ux-pattern-analysis-loading-feedback>loading patterns</a> and what else you need to keep in mind to design an appropriate loading feedback experience.</p></div></article></div><div class=f-article-item><article class=article--post><header><div class="article--post__image rounded-lg w-20 h-20"><figure role=presentation class=bio-image><a href=https://uk.linkedin.com/in/mattzeunert class=bio-image-link><div class=bio-image-wrapper><img class=bio-image-image src=https://files.smashing.media/community-links/matt-zeunert-100px-opt.png loading=eager decoding=async fetchpriority=high width=100 height=100 alt="Matt Zeunert"></div></a></figure></div><span class=article--post__author-name><a class=red href=https://uk.linkedin.com/in/mattzeunert>Matt Zeunert</a>
<em class=light-grey>wrote</em></span></header><h2 class="article--post__title h1"><a href=https://www.debugbear.com/blog/web-performance-user-experience>How Web Performance Impacts UX</a></h2><div class=article--post__content><p class=article--post__teaser><time datetime=2026-02-04 class=article--post__time>February 4, 2026 —</time>
How do response times impact user experience and behavior? And how can you measure performance and business metrics? Matt Zeunert wrote a <a href=https://www.debugbear.com/blog/web-performance-user-experience>guide</a> exploring the role speed plays for website visitors.</p></div></article></div><div class=f-article-item><article class=article--post><header><div class="article--post__image rounded-lg w-20 h-20"><figure role=presentation class=bio-image><a href=https://linkedin.com/in/greghuntoon class=bio-image-link><div class=bio-image-wrapper><img class=bio-image-image src=https://files.smashing.media/community-links/greg-huntoon-100px-opt.png loading=eager decoding=async fetchpriority=high width=100 height=100 alt="Greg Huntoon"></div></a></figure></div><span class=article--post__author-name><a class=red href=https://linkedin.com/in/greghuntoon>Greg Huntoon</a>
<em class=light-grey>wrote</em></span></header><h2 class="article--post__title h1"><a href=https://www.figma.com/blog/designer-framework-for-better-ai-prompts/>Better AI Prompts</a></h2><div class=article--post__content><p class=article--post__teaser><time datetime=2026-02-03 class=article--post__time>February 3, 2026 —</time>
How can designers write better prompts? Greg Huntoon shares a <a href=https://www.figma.com/blog/designer-framework-for-better-ai-prompts/>framework</a> for structuring prompts to strengthen intent and turn AI into a reliable design partner.</p></div></article></div><div class=f-article-item><article class=article--post><header><div class="article--post__image rounded-lg w-20 h-20"><figure role=presentation class=bio-image><a href=https://uk.linkedin.com/in/adrian-raudaschl class=bio-image-link><div class=bio-image-wrapper><img class=bio-image-image src=https://files.smashing.media/community-links/adrian-raudaschl-100px-opt.png loading=eager decoding=async fetchpriority=high width=100 height=100 alt="Adrian Raudaschl"></div></a></figure></div><span class=article--post__author-name><a class=red href=https://uk.linkedin.com/in/adrian-raudaschl>Adrian Raudaschl</a>
<em class=light-grey>wrote</em></span></header><h2 class="article--post__title h1"><a href=https://uxdesign.cc/tars-a-product-metric-game-changer-c523f260306a>TARS Framework</a></h2><div class=article--post__content><p class=article--post__teaser><time datetime=2026-02-02 class=article--post__time>February 2, 2026 —</time>
How do you know if your shiny new product feature actually works for your end users? The <a href=https://uxdesign.cc/tars-a-product-metric-game-changer-c523f260306a>TARS framework</a> helps you evaluate feature performance beyond revenue and business-level metrics like NPS.</p></div></article></div><div class=f-article-item><article class=article--post><header><div class="article--post__image rounded-lg w-20 h-20"><figure role=presentation class=bio-image><a href=https://www.linkedin.com/in/emanuelagorla/ class=bio-image-link><div class=bio-image-wrapper><img class=bio-image-image src=https://files.smashing.media/community-links/ela-gorla-100px-opt.png loading=eager decoding=async fetchpriority=high width=100 height=100 alt="Ela Gorla"></div></a></figure></div><span class=article--post__author-name><a class=red href=https://www.linkedin.com/in/emanuelagorla/>Ela Gorla</a>
<em class=light-grey>wrote</em></span></header><h2 class="article--post__title h1"><a href=https://tetralogical.com/blog/2026/01/07/common-misconceptions-about-testing-accessibility/>Accessibility Testing Misconceptions</a></h2><div class=article--post__content><p class=article--post__teaser><time datetime=2026-01-30 class=article--post__time>January 30, 2026 —</time>
Assessing the most effective approach for testing your product’s accessibility can be challenging, given the wide range of tools and methodologies available. Ela Gorla examines <a href=https://tetralogical.com/blog/2026/01/07/common-misconceptions-about-testing-accessibility/>common misconceptions</a> and how to address them.</p></div></article></div><div class=f-article-item><article class=article--post><header><div class="article--post__image rounded-lg w-20 h-20"><figure role=presentation class=bio-image><a href=https://www.linkedin.com/in/annalahey class=bio-image-link><div class=bio-image-wrapper><img class=bio-image-image src=https://files.smashing.media/community-links/anna-kaley-100px-opt.png loading=eager decoding=async fetchpriority=high width=100 height=100 alt="Anna Kaley"></div></a></figure></div><span class=article--post__author-name><a class=red href=https://www.linkedin.com/in/annalahey>Anna Kaley</a>
<em class=light-grey>wrote</em></span></header><h2 class="article--post__title h1"><a href=https://www.nngroup.com/articles/listbox-dropdown/>Listboxes vs. Dropdown Lists</a></h2><div class=article--post__content><p class=article--post__teaser><time datetime=2026-01-29 class=article--post__time>January 29, 2026 —</time>
Listboxes and dropdowns allow users to select options. But when to use which? Anna Kaley discusses <a href=https://www.nngroup.com/articles/listbox-dropdown/>when to use each element</a> and cases where either will suffice.</p></div></article></div></div><div class=col-12><div class=load-more><a class=load-more__link href=https://www.twitter.com/smashingmag>More links on Twitter</a></div></div></div></div></section></main><div data-component=CookieBanner></div><div id=cart class=cart-wrapper data-component=MiniCart></div><footer class=main-footer><div class=container><div class=col-12><div class="footer__topics open"><h4 class=footer__topics__title id=topics>Browse All Smashing Magazine Topics</h4><ul class=footer__topics__list><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/accessibility>Accessibility</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/best-practices>Best practices</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/business>Business</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/career>Career</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/checklists>Checklists</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/css>CSS</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/data-visualization>Data Visualization</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/design>Design</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/design-patterns>Design Patterns</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/design-systems>Design Systems</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/e-commerce>E-Commerce</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/figma>Figma</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/freebies>Freebies</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/html>HTML</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/illustrator>Illustrator</a></li><li class=footer__topics__item><a href=/category/inspiration>Inspiration</a></li><li cl